SUMMARY:Good Grief: A 4-part Writing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Good Grief: a 4-part writing workshop with Professor Alexandra 
 Dos SantosMondays\, 7:00 - 9:00 @ Olio LighthouseJan 18th\, 25th\, Feb 1st
 \, 8th “Grief is just love with no place to go.”&nbsp\;So writes autho
 r Jamie Anderson when describing how it felt to lose her mother. This clas
 s is designed to give your grief a place to go: art\, which is perhaps the
  only realm capable of holding the enormity\, complexity\, and incomprehen
 sibility of grief. This will be a safe space with a supportive community\,
  where we will connect not only with those we grieve\, but with one anothe
 r. As the poet Rumi writes\, "The wound is the place where the light enter
 s you.”&nbsp\;Workshop Layout:This Olio 4-part will offer a variety of c
 urated works for discussion to help us gain perspective on grief’s tende
 rness and depth. Each week we’ll explore some poetry\, fiction\, paintin
 gs\, performance art\, and/or music. The group will also be invited to bri
 ng in a work that they want to share during the last session.We’ll parti
 cipate in writing activities to give our grief texture and form. There wil
 l be an optional group/partner feedback portion\, but you may simply liste
 n if you do not wish to share. By the end of the 4-weeks you'll have done 
 one of the most important things a human being can do with their grief - e
 xpress it.&nbsp\;Who can take this class?Anyone carrying grief in their he
 art. Whether you lost a job\, relationship\, pet\, loved one\, or old way 
 of life\, there is a space for you here.&nbsp\;You don’t need to be a wr
 iter to benefit from the discussion and exercises in this class. It will b
 e a low-pressure environment with priority placed on communal discovery an
 d healing. While the generative exercises will focus primarily on writing\
 , you may also interpret the prompts to create visual art&nbsp\; or music 
 if you work in a different medium. Just bring your materials along.Mondays
 \, 7:30 - 9:30&nbsp\;Jan 18. WEEK 1: PoetryAndrea Gibson\, Mary Oliver\, O
 cean Vuong and more.&nbsp\;Jan. 25 WEEK 2: Visual and Performance ArtFrida
  Kahlo\, August Friedrich Schenck\, Marina Abramović\, and more&nbsp\;Feb
  1. WEEK 3: Fiction and EssaysToni Morrison\, CS Lewis\, and moreFeb 8. WE
 EK 4: Open MediumOptional peer-led shares of chosen grief worksAbout Your 
 Instructor:Alexandra Dos Santos is a Pushcart Award nominated writer and p
 rofessor based in Astoria\, New York. Influenced by horror films\, the eso
 teric\, and fairytales\, her writing explores grief\, addiction\, depressi
 on\, and other fun topics. Her work has appeared in The Rumpus\, Split Lip
  Magazine\, Electric Literature\, Lithub\, Flash Fiction Magazine\, Vol. 1
  Brooklyn\, among others. She's led creative writing workshops throughout 
 Brooklyn and received fellowships from Wildacres Writers Retreat and the D
 isquiet International Literary Program.*Writers of all levels are welcome 
 here! Reach out to David@thinkolio.org if price is a barrier for you.\n\nT
 ickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/good_grief_a_4part
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/good_grief_a_4part
END:VEVENT
